SUMMARY:Pokémon GO Wild Area 2026: Sendai • Tohoku
DTSTART:20261106T010000Z
DTEND:20261108T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:GO Wild Area returns in 2026 with Steel- and Dragon-type Pokém
 on\, the debuts of Dynamax Dialga and Dynamax Palkia\, and powerful mighty
  Pokémon. Collect GO Safari Balls to help catch these challenging encount
 ers!\nDates: November 6\, 7\, or 8\, 2026 Time: 10:00 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. J
 ST (UTC+9) Location: Sendai\, Japan\, with gameplay throughout Miyagi Pref
 ecture Ticket: ¥4\,000 (including applicable taxes and fees) for one day\
 nAll event gameplay is exclusive to ticket holders. A standard ticket cove
 rs one selected day\; Extra Day add-ons extend eligible gameplay to additi
 onal days. Gameplay is available only within the event area at the date an
 d time specified on your ticket.\nTicket registration: Register from Septe
 mber 11 at 8:00 a.m. JST through September 15\, 2026\, at 7:59 a.m. JST. R
 egistered Trainers will be notified of their purchase window afterward. Ti
 ckets are first come\, first served\, and registration does not guarantee 
 availability. Read the ticket registration announcement.\n\n▸ Related Ev
 ents\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n▸ Ticket Holder Bonuses\nThe following bo
 nuses apply from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. local time on your ticketed event
  day.\n• Increased chance to encounter Shiny Pokémon\n• 1/2 Hatch Dis
 tance for Eggs placed in Incubators during the event\n• Up to 10 free Ra
 id Passes per day from Gyms\n• 3/4 Max Particle cost for unlocking and p
 owering up Max Moves\n• Daily Max Particle collection limit increased to
  8\,000\n• Increased Max Particles from Power Spots and exploration\n•
  Increased chance of 10 km Eggs from PokéStops and Gyms\n• Lure Modules
  last for 2 hours\n• Incense\, excluding Daily Adventure Incense\, lasts
  for 2 hours\n• 2× Candy for catching Pokémon\n• Party Play lasts fo
 r 8 hours\n• Chance to encounter mighty Pokémon on Routes\n• 3 GO Sna
 pshot surprise encounters per day\n• Chance to get GO Safari Balls from 
 PokéStops and Gyms\n\n▸ Trading Bonuses\nTicket holders receive these b
 enefits from 12:00 a.m. to 11:59 p.m. local time on their ticketed event d
 ay.\n• Up to 6 Special Trades per day\n• 1/2 Stardust cost for trades\
 nShiny encounters are not guaranteed. To use the increased exploration Max
  Particle bonus\, first collect all available Max Particles in the Nearby 
 menu. Adventure Sync can help track exploration distance.\n\n━━ FEATUR
 ES ━━\n▸ Dynamax Dialga and Dynamax Palkia\nDynamax Dialga and Dynam
 ax Palkia make their Pokémon GO debuts during GO Wild Area 2026. Both can
  be Shiny!\nBoth Pokémon will appear in Max Battles during the in-person 
 event.\n\n▸ Machamp Wearing a Modern Jacket\nA new costumed Machamp appe
 ars in three-star raids during the event. Lucky Trainers may encounter a S
 hiny one! Ticket holders can also encounter this Machamp as a mighty Poké
 mon in the wild.\n\n▸ Hisuian Sliggoo and Hisuian Goodra Debut\nHisuian 
 Sliggoo and Hisuian Goodra debut at the in-person GO Wild Area events. Tic
 ket holders may find Hisuian Sliggoo in the wild during either habitat hou
 r\, including its Shiny form.\nUse 100 Goomy Candy to evolve Hisuian Sligg
 oo into Hisuian Goodra.\nPokémon: Hisuian Sliggoo\, Hisuian Goodra\n\n▸
  Mighty Latias and Latios\nTicket holders may attract mighty Latias and La
 tios with Incense\, excluding Daily Adventure Incense\, on their ticketed 
 event day. Both can be Shiny and are quick to flee\, so keep GO Safari Bal
 ls ready.\n\n▸ GO Safari Balls\nGO Safari Balls improve the chance of ca
 tching Pokémon\, especially mighty Pokémon. Ticket holders can obtain th
 em by spinning PokéStops and Gym Photo Discs during event hours.\nThey ca
 n only be used from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. local time on event days and b
 ecome inaccessible after the event ends.\n\n▸ Supply Balloons\nTicket ho
 lders receive hourly Supply Balloons with GO Safari Balls during event hou
 rs.\n\n▸ GO Snapshot\, Routes\, and Party Play\nTake snapshots for surpr
 ise encounters with Steel- and Dragon-type Pokémon. Explore Routes for a 
 chance to find mighty Pokémon\, and enjoy Party Play sessions lasting eig
 ht hours.\n\n▸ In-Person Experiences\nGameplay extends throughout Miyagi
  Prefecture\, with in-person activities centered in Sendai.\n\n▸ Pop-Ups
  and Photo Opportunities\nVisit event pop-ups to meet other Trainers and e
 njoy themed photo opportunities. Exact pop-up locations will be announced 
 later.\n\n▸ Community Hub\n…\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Rotating Hab
 itat Hours\nSteel- and Dragon-themed encounters rotate hourly from 10:00 a
 .m. to 6:00 p.m. throughout the event area on your ticketed day.\n\n▸ So
 lid as Steel Hour\n10:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m. 12:00 p.m. to 1:00 p.m. 2:00 p
 .m. to 3:00 p.m. 4:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m.\nPokémon: Alolan Sandshrew\, Alol
 an Diglett\, Magnemite\, Shellder\, Onix\, Porygon\, Shuckle\, Skarmory\, 
 Nosepass\, Aron\, Beldum\, Piplup\, Shieldon\, Bronzor\, Lucario\, Drilbur
 \, Ferroseed\, Klink\, Galarian Stunfisk\, Durant\, Hisuian Sliggoo\, Rook
 idee\, Tinkatink\, Orthworm\n\n▸ Daring as Dragons Hour\n11:00 a.m. to 1
 2:00 p.m. 1:00 p.m. to 2:00 p.m. 3:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. 5:00 p.m. to 6:00 
 p.m.\nPokémon: Charmander\, Magikarp\, Dratini\, Gligar\, Trapinch\, Swab
 lu\, Barboach\, Bagon\, Gible\, Tynamo\, Axew\, Heatmor\, Deino\, Skrelp\,
  Tyrunt\, Amaura\, Goomy\, Hisuian Sliggoo\, Noibat\, Turtonator\, Jangmo-
 o\, Applin\, Sizzlipede\, Frigibax\n\n▸ Mighty Pokémon\nMighty Pokémon
  are more likely to have high Attack\, Defense\, and HP ratings and be XL 
 or XXL. They are harder to catch\, and some may be Shiny. GO Safari Balls 
 improve your chances of catching them.\nMighty Pokémon can appear during 
 either habitat hour. The in-person lineup includes mighty Machamp wearing 
 a modern jacket\, Bastiodon\, and Kommo-o\, plus mighty Lapras in Sendai.\
 nPokémon: Modern Jacket Machamp\, Alolan Exeggutor\, Lapras\, Azumarill\,
  Scizor\, Kingdra\, Aggron\, Flygon\, Walrein\, Metagross\, Empoleon\, Bas
 tiodon\, Magnezone\, Conkeldurr\, Ferrothorn\, Haxorus\, Hydreigon\, Goodr
 a\, Noivern\, Kommo-o\, Tinkaton\, Clodsire\n\n▸ Incense Encounters\nTic
 ket holders can attract the following mighty Pokémon during the event. Th
 ese encounters exclude Daily Adventure Incense.\nPokémon: Lapras\, Azumar
 ill\, Scizor\, Kingdra\, Aggron\, Flygon\, Empoleon\, Bastiodon\, Conkeldu
 rr\, Hydreigon\, Kommo-o\n\n…\n\n…
